    {
      "id": 62,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1515.7408387883006,
        -1220.520365103764
      ],
      "size": [
        439.92987728524963,
        416.3277402120399
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 6,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Overview",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.7",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 🎬✨ Video Watermark Removal\n\nRemove annoying watermarks from your video automatically, frame by frame. Especially useful for Sora-style watermarks. It's not perfect and can leave behind some artifacts, but it's fast and gets the job done.\n\n## 🧠 How it works\n\n1. 🎥 **Load Video**  \n   Splits your video into frames and keeps the original audio.\n\n2. 🔍 **Detect Watermark (SAM3)**  \n   Uses `SAM3Segment` with the prompt **\"watermark\"** to find the watermark in each frame and generate a mask.\n\n3. 🫧 **Mask Refine**  \n   The mask is grown and feathered so coverage is solid and edges blend smoothly. Press **AUTO** on the node to size both for your video.\n\n4. 🧼 **Remove Watermark**  \n   The refined mask is passed into `LaMa Inpaint 🆎` using `big-lama.pt`.\n\n5. 🎞️ **Rebuild Video**  \n   Frames are stitched back together with the original audio and FPS preserved.\n\n## 📦 Model setup\n\nPlace `big-lama.pt` at `ComfyUI/models/lama/big-lama.pt`, then restart ComfyUI. The AusBoss node never downloads models automatically.\n\n## 💡 Notes\n\n- ✅ Works best with consistent/static watermarks\n- 🪶 Feathering helps avoid ugly edges\n- 📦 Outputs H.264 MP4 by default; Save Video also writes h265, webm, ProRes, lossless and gif/webp\n\n## 📦 Requires\n\n- 🧩 **ComfyUI-AusBoss** — Load Video, Select Frame, Mask Refine, LaMa Inpaint, Image Compare A/B, Save Video\n- 🧩 **ComfyUI-RMBG** — SAM3 segmentation\n- 🧩 **rgthree-comfy** — labels and the group toggles\n- 🧩 **ComfyUI-Easy-Use** — the Total Frames readout\n- 📥 **Model**: a TorchScript `big-lama.pt` in `ComfyUI/models/lama/`"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# 🎬✨ Video Watermark Removal\n\nRemove annoying watermarks from your video automatically, frame by frame. Especially useful for Sora-style watermarks. It's not perfect and can leave behind some artifacts, but it's fast and gets the job done.\n\n## 🧠 How it works\n\n1. 🎥 **Load Video**  \n   Splits your video into frames and keeps the original audio.\n\n2. 🔍 **Detect Watermark (SAM3)**  \n   Uses `SAM3Segment` with the prompt **\"watermark\"** to find the watermark in each frame and generate a mask.\n\n3. 🫧 **Mask Refine**  \n   The mask is grown and feathered so coverage is solid and edges blend smoothly. Press **AUTO** on the node to size both for your video.\n\n4. 🧼 **Remove Watermark**  \n   The refined mask is passed into `LaMa Inpaint 🆎` using `big-lama.pt`.\n\n5. 🎞️ **Rebuild Video**  \n   Frames are stitched back together with the original audio and FPS preserved.\n\n## 📦 Model setup\n\nPlace `big-lama.pt` at `ComfyUI/models/lama/big-lama.pt`, then restart ComfyUI. The AusBoss node never downloads models automatically.\n\n## 💡 Notes\n\n- ✅ Works best with consistent/static watermarks\n- 🪶 Feathering helps avoid ugly edges\n- 📦 Outputs H.264 MP4 by default; Save Video also writes h265, webm, ProRes, lossless and gif/webp\n\n## 📦 Requires\n\n- 🧩 **ComfyUI-AusBoss** — Load Video, Select Frame, Mask Refine, LaMa Inpaint, Image Compare A/B, Save Video\n- 🧩 **ComfyUI-RMBG** — SAM3 segmentation\n- 🧩 **rgthree-comfy** — labels and the group toggles\n- 🧩 **ComfyUI-Easy-Use** — the Total Frames readout\n- 📥 **Model**: a TorchScript `big-lama.pt` in `ComfyUI/models/lama/`"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
